mission "The Quiet Passenger"
    category "side"
    name "The Quiet Passenger"
    description "Give a discreet passage to a retired teacher travelling to Saint's Refuge."
    source "Santa Isabela"
    destination "Saint's Refuge"
    reward 540
    speaker offer "Professor Alvaro Mendes"
    speaker visit "Sister Maud"
    speaker complete "Sister Maud"
    on offer
        conversation
            `An elderly man with a neat grey beard asks for a passage. He has one small trunk, a walking stick, and no desire to explain himself to the customs officers.`
            `"I taught navigation at the academy for thirty years. I have retired, and would prefer to spend what remains of my time somewhere quiet. Saint's Refuge has offered me a room. I can pay a fair fare, and I promise not to complain about the ship's cooking."`
            choice
                `"There is room aboard. Welcome, professor."`
                    accept
                `"I am not sailing that way."`
                    close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Quiet Passenger. Carry Professor Alvaro Mendes to Saint's Refuge."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Sister Maud greets the professor by name and takes his trunk. "We have his room ready. The children have been waiting for someone to teach them their letters."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `The professor pays his fare and leaves a folded chart in your cabin: a tidy set of notes on currents around the Outer Antilles. It is not treasure, but it may prove useful.`
